  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-gitea-2026-79960",
  "summary": "Gitea deploy key pushes acting as the repository owner",
  "details": "When a push was authenticated with a deploy key, Gitea recorded the repository owner as the pusher, so permission checks in the push hook pipeline evaluated the owner instead of the deploy key. A holder of a writable deploy key could create protected tags without being on the tag allow list and change repository visibility through push options, for example making a private repository public. Pull requests created through the AGit flow with a deploy key were also attributed to the owner.",
